  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hainanese chicken rice is three things at once: a poaching technique, a rice method, and a set of dipping sauces. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "gentle-poaching"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "gentle poaching"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " keeps the chicken moist. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ice-bath"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ice bath"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sets the skin. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chicken-rice-fat"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chicken fat"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flavours the rice. All three matter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The dipping sauces are as important as the chicken itself. At minimum, serve ginger paste and a chilli sauce alongside. Oyster sauce thinned with a little hot stock makes a simple third option."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
